{"id":"84dce5217e459217","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-local-zeta.md","title":"Local Zeta Function","display":"df-local-zeta — Local Zeta Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-local-zeta","aliases":["58-df-local-zeta","Local Zeta Function"],"display":"df-local-zeta — Local Zeta Function","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-local-field.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-local-zeta"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-local-zeta</span><span>Local Zeta Function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-local-zeta — Local Zeta Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9e19ee25a61be95f\" href=\"?note=9e19ee25a61be95f\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-local-field.md\">../batch11/58-df-local-field.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"82cd211c4765302c\" href=\"?note=82cd211c4765302c\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md\">../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"z,K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k,G_K,\\mu^\\times,\\phi,\\chi,s\\in V\">\\(z,K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k,G_K,\\mu^\\times,\\phi,\\chi,s\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LocalField}_S\\subseteq V^9\">\\(\\mathrm{LocalField}_S\\subseteq V^9\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9e19ee25a61be95f\" href=\"?note=9e19ee25a61be95f\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-local-field.md\">../batch11/58-df-local-field.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8HaarMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8HaarMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"82cd211c4765302c\" href=\"?note=82cd211c4765302c\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md\">../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LocalZeta}_S\\subseteq V^{15}\">\\(\\mathrm{LocalZeta}_S\\subseteq V^{15}\\)</span> is the local-zeta-value graph defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}local\\text{-}zeta}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LocalZeta}_S(z,K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k,G_K,\\mu^\\times,\\phi,\\chi,s)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LocalField}_S(K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists m_K,i_K,\\tau_v\\in V\\;\\Bigl[\nm_K=\\{\\langle\\langle x,y\\rangle,x\\cdot_Ky\\rangle:x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land i_K=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle:x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\land x\\cdot_Ky=1_K\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_v=\\Bigl\\{U\\subseteq K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}:\n\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\Bigl((y=x\\lor\n(y+_K(-_Kx)\\neq0_K\\land v(y+_K(-_Kx))\\geq n))\\to y\\in U\\Bigr)\\Bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land G_K=\\langle K\\setminus\\{0_K\\},m_K,1_K,i_K,\\tau_v\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8HaarMeasure}_S(\\mu^\\times,G_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\phi,K,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\chi,K\\setminus\\{0_K\\},\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\})\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\n\\chi(x\\cdot_Ky)=\\chi(x)\\chi(y)\n\\land\\forall x\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{29mm}\\Bigl((y=x\\lor\n(y+_K(-_Kx)\\neq0_K\\land v(y+_K(-_Kx))\\geq n))\n\\to |\\chi(y)-\\chi(x)|&lt;\\varepsilon\\Bigr)\n\\land s,z\\in\\mathbb C\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\int_{K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}}\n\\left|\\phi(x)\\chi(x)|k|^{-s\\,v(x)}\\right|\\,d\\mu^\\times(x)&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land z=\\int_{K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}}\n\\phi(x)\\chi(x)|k|^{-s\\,v(x)}\\,d\\mu^\\times(x)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}local\\text{-}zeta}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LocalZeta}_S(z,K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k,G_K,\\mu^\\times,\\phi,\\chi,s)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{LocalField}_S(K,+_K,\\cdot_K,0_K,1_K,v,\\mathcal O_K,\\mathfrak m_K,k)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists m_K,i_K,\\tau_v\\in V\\;\\Bigl[\nm_K=\\{\\langle\\langle x,y\\rangle,x\\cdot_Ky\\rangle:x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land i_K=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle:x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\land x\\cdot_Ky=1_K\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_v=\\Bigl\\{U\\subseteq K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}:\n\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\Bigl((y=x\\lor\n(y+_K(-_Kx)\\neq0_K\\land v(y+_K(-_Kx))\\geq n))\\to y\\in U\\Bigr)\\Bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land G_K=\\langle K\\setminus\\{0_K\\},m_K,1_K,i_K,\\tau_v\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure8HaarMeasure}_S(\\mu^\\times,G_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\phi,K,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\chi,K\\setminus\\{0_K\\},\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\})\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall x,y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\n\\chi(x\\cdot_Ky)=\\chi(x)\\chi(y)\n\\land\\forall x\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall y\\in K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}\\;\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{29mm}\\Bigl((y=x\\lor\n(y+_K(-_Kx)\\neq0_K\\land v(y+_K(-_Kx))\\geq n))\n\\to |\\chi(y)-\\chi(x)|&lt;\\varepsilon\\Bigr)\n\\land s,z\\in\\mathbb C\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\int_{K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}}\n\\left|\\phi(x)\\chi(x)|k|^{-s\\,v(x)}\\right|\\,d\\mu^\\times(x)&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land z=\\int_{K\\setminus\\{0_K\\}}\n\\phi(x)\\chi(x)|k|^{-s\\,v(x)}\\,d\\mu^\\times(x)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the value graph of Tate's local zeta integral; meromorphic continuation and the local functional equation are downstream theorems.</li>\n<li>The field operations, valuation topology, multiplicative group, Haar measure, continuous character, exponent and evaluation point are all explicit. Absolute integrability is part of the graph's domain condition; the usual Schwartz--Bruhat restriction on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\phi\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> may be imposed by a downstream specialization. The earlier formula called a nine-place local-field predicate with five arguments and left <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d^\\times x\">\\(d^\\times x\\)</span> unbound.</li>\n<li>Unramified: inertia acts trivially; Frobenius eigenvalues =Satake parameters</li>\n<li>Ramified: conductor <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{f}(\\chi)\">\\(\\mathfrak{f}(\\chi)\\)</span>; twisted by additive character</li>\n<li>Langlands: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_v(s, \\pi_v) = L_v(s, \\rho \\circ \\sigma_v)\">\\(L_v(s, \\pi_v) = L_v(s, \\rho \\circ \\sigma_v)\\)</span> for representation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\rho\">\\(\\rho\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bushnell and Henniart, The Local Langlands Conjecture for GL(2)</li>\n<li>Tate, Number Theoretic Background</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-local-field.md","status":"resolved","id":"9e19ee25a61be95f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-local-field.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"82cd211c4765302c","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-local-field.md","status":"resolved","id":"9e19ee25a61be95f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LocalField}_S\\subseteq V^9$ (see [[../batch11/58-df-local-field.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3$ (see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-zfc-measure8-haar-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"82cd211c4765302c","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mat